<article class="env-lemma" id="0GNJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GNJ">Lemma <span data-tag="0GNJ">56.2.1</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a ring. Let $\mathcal{B}$ be a category having filtered colimits. Let $F : \text{Mod}^{fp}_ A \to \mathcal{B}$ be a functor. Then $F$ extends uniquely to a functor $F' : \text{Mod}_ A \to \mathcal{B}$ which commutes with filtered colimits. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/0FWY" data-tag="0FWY">4.26.2</a>. To see that the lemma applies observe that finitely presented $A$-modules are categorically compact objects of $\text{Mod}_ A$ by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0G8P" data-tag="0G8P">10.11.4</a>. Also, every $A$-module is a filtered colimit of finitely presented $A$-modules by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00HA" data-tag="00HA">10.11.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>